### Problem description & steps to reproduce

## What's going on?

When using chat format "Hermes 2 Pro" with tools enabled, llama-server may incorrectly interpret normal assistant output that contains JSON (or JSON embedded in code) as a tool call. This occurs even when the model does not emit `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` (or any tool-call tag). In streaming mode, the parser can attempt to parse incomplete JSON, trigger JSON-healing, and emit a spurious `tool_calls` delta / `finish_reason: "tool_calls"`.

I noticed this after my model attempted to output some sample code and instead performed a tool call to a non-existent tool.

## Expected Behavior

Tool calls should only be parsed when explicitly denoted by the expected wrapper for the template (e.g. `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` or `<function=...>...</function>`), or at minimum only when the parsed JSON matches an actual tool schema/name. Normal JSON or code snippets in assistant content must not be interpreted as tool calls.

## Actual Behavior

* The Hermes 2 Pro parser matches any occurrence of `{ "name": ...` in assistant output, even when not wrapped in `<tool_call>` / `<function_call>` tags.
* In streaming mode, this can become a “partial tool call” when the JSON is incomplete mid-generation, triggering JSON healing and producing spurious tool call metadata.

