### Problem description & steps to reproduce

When a tool schema includes an array-typed parameter and the model generates string values containing `{` or `}` characters, the `function.arguments` field in the response has that array serialized as a JSON-encoded string instead of a JSON array.

This breaks any client that parses and validates tool arguments against the schema, as the type of `edits` changes from `array` to `string` depending on the content of the values, not the schema.

The model's own reasoning seems to show it understands that it expected the tool argument to be an array but the serialized output is wrong when shown the error. 

#### Suspected Diagnosis (from Claude after some long debugging session)

The log line `Chat format: peg-gemma4` indicates the PEG grammar parser is active for tool call extraction on this model. The failure pattern — triggered specifically by `{` / `}` characters inside string values — is consistent with the `<|"|>` delimiter token issue described in #21316. PR #21327 was understood to address this, but the bug persists at commit `af5c13841fb9`. It is possible the PEG grammar's dict-value parser still mishandles the delimiter tokens when they appear inside array element string values, falling back to serializing the entire array as a raw string.


#### Context on where I faced this issue
This is an example interaction from [pi-mono](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono), which validates tool arguments strictly against the schema:

```
 > I need you to test the edit tool. Create a test code file (a hello world) and try to edit it                                                

 write hello.py                                                                                                                              

 print("Hello, World!")                                                                                                                      



 edit hello.py                                                                                                                               

 Validation failed for tool "edit":                                                                                                          
   - edits: must be array                                                                                                                    

 Received arguments:                                                                                                                         
 {                                                                                                                                           
   "edits": "[{\"newText\":\"print(\"Hello, \"Pi!\")<|\"|>,oldText\":\"print(\"Hello, \"World!\")<|\"|>}]\"",                                
   "path": "hello.py"                                                                                                                        
 }     
```

Note the `<|"|>` tokens leaking into the output - the same issue reported in #21316.


